**Read:** Complete the surface and contact readings, then follow the original papers needed for each comparison. The three investigations can share the same chosen object while asking different questions.

Connect a contact-mechanics calculation, a wetting or humidity observation and a surface-population account. Each study requires derivation, a stated measurement chain, alternatives and limits. Assigned source reading is broader than the passages inspected during this pathway's construction.

**Work:** Carry out all three investigations at increasing depth. Begin with the supplied hypothetical cases, then reconstruct a published result using its actual conditions. When data or apparatus are unavailable, identify the missing evidence and present a reproducible analysis of the stated model without inventing experimental validation.

